      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for making so many comments. After seeing this, I realized that we heavily rely on the assumption that both `ctx` and `d` (`dexpreopter`) are about a single library, and your previous changes actually broke that assumption. Here are my suggestions:\n\n1. [`dexpreopter`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/java/dexpreopt.go;l\u003d101;drc\u003d5be6333692b6881b223b672c2251efaf4605bb33) has too many fields about a single library, so it\u0027s very hard to change it. You need to create one `dexpreopter` per library in `dexpreoptSystemServerJars`, or things won\u0027t work on an apex that provides multiple libraries ([`example`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/AdServices/apex/Android.bp;l\u003d55-56;drc\u003d614f36a36c1dbce49118f7113a7c075a4de29663)).\n\n2. You need to check all the usages of `ctx` in this file to see if they still makes sense when `ctx` represents an apex.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 219,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 219,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "96db41c57d2ed540c0ceddf0687938081faee7d4",
