      "writtenOn": "2024-01-26T01:24:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like you are adding the `libName` parameter to too many functions. In this case, I think it makes more sense to add `libName` as a field in `dexpreopter` rather than a parameter. You can also add a check at the beginning of `dexpreopter.dexpreopt()` to make sure the `libName` field is set, and panic if it isn\u0027t.\n\nIn order to do so, you need to refactor the code **before this CL** to have 1:1 mapping between `dexpreopter` and java library, rather than doing it in a followup CL. You probably need to remove `dexpreopter` from struct `prebuiltCommon`, and instead, create a `dexpreopter` for each library in the loop in `dexpreoptSystemServerJars`. This will make `prebuiltCommon` no longer satisfy `DexpreopterInterface`, but that\u0027s okay because `DexpreopterInterface` doesn\u0027t make sense for `prebuiltCommon` anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "c447e085_8e25241d",
      "range": {
